text:
What you are looking at. Six investment rules are fitted on the same monthly stock panel and turned into holdings with a common portfolio formula. The chart follows one dollar invested in each rule on a unit-gross basis. Switching the view to beta-only vs complete IAB isolates one decision inside NA-IPCA, the use of the retained intercept mean, by capitalisation universe. The ablation ladder shows, within one fitted model, how much of the gross increment comes from the mean input rather than the instability adjustment. Which of these choices moves the wealth path, and by how much?

palette = ({
  naipca_iab: "#18557f", complete: "#18557f",
  qz_ipca: "#8a6a1a",
  ipca: "#6f9cc0", rp_pca: "#7a7a7a", ff5: "#b3b3b3",
  naipca_beta_only: "#8a8378", beta_only: "#8a8378",
  band: "rgba(0,0,0,0.06)", muted: "rgba(0,0,0,0.6)", rule: "rgba(0,0,0,0.1)"
})
LANG = (document.documentElement.lang || "en").startsWith("zh") ? "zh" : "en"
STR = ({ en: { view: "View", cost: "Cost (bp per traded dollar)", universe: "Universe", sample: "Sample (months)", log: "Log scale", models: "Models", statistic: "Statistic", theme: "Theme", sort: "Sort by", method: "Method", scenario: "Scenario", block: "Block (months)", metric: "Metric", intervals: "Intervals", cost_bp: "One-way cost (bp)", failed: "Interactive data failed to load. The static figure is shown instead." },
        zh: { view: "视图", cost: "成本（每交易一美元，基点）", universe: "股票池", sample: "样本（月）", log: "对数坐标", models: "模型", statistic: "统计量", theme: "主题", sort: "排序", method: "方法", scenario: "情景", block: "块长（月）", metric: "指标", intervals: "区间", cost_bp: "单边成本（基点）", failed: "交互数据加载失败，改为显示静态图。" } })
t = (k) =&gt; STR[LANG][k] ?? STR.en[k] ?? k
fmt2 = (x) =&gt; (x == null || Number.isNaN(x)) ? "n/a" : x.toFixed(2)
fmt1 = (x) =&gt; (x == null || Number.isNaN(x)) ? "n/a" : x.toFixed(1)
fmtBp = (x) =&gt; (x == null || Number.isNaN(x)) ? "&gt; 500" : `${Math.round(x)} bp`
parseMonth = (s) =&gt; new Date(`${s}-01T00:00:00Z`)
// Sharpe, annualised, sample std (ddof = 1): matches the release convention
sharpe = (r) =&gt; {
  const n = r.length, m = r.reduce((a, b) =&gt; a + b, 0) / n
  const v = r.reduce((a, b) =&gt; a + (b - m) ** 2, 0) / (n - 1)
  const vol = Math.sqrt(v) * Math.sqrt(12)
  return vol &gt; 1e-12 ? (m * 12) / vol : NaN
}
netSeries = (r, to, bp) =&gt; r.map((x, i) =&gt; x - to[i] * bp / 1e4)
wealthPath = (r) =&gt; { let w = 1; return r.map((x) =&gt; (w *= 1 + x)) }
nberMarks = (nber) =&gt; Plot.rectX(nber, { x1: (d) =&gt; parseMonth(d.start), x2: (d) =&gt; parseMonth(d.end), fill: palette.band })























































































Figure 1: Portfolio formation under alternative factor models. Cumulative wealth from one dollar on a unit-gross basis, CORE universe, June 1973 to November 2024 (618 months).


pf_data = FileAttachment("/data/portfolio_formation.json").json().catch(() =&gt; null)
pf_loadFailed = pf_data === null ? html`&lt;p class="figcaption"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;${t("failed")}&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;img src="/assets/img/portfolio_formation.png" alt="Cumulative unit-gross wealth of six factor-model portfolios, CORE universe, 1973 to 2024, log scale, NBER recessions shaded" style="width:100%"&gt;` : html``
















viewof pf_view = Inputs.radio(new Map([["Across models", "cross"], ["Beta-only vs complete IAB", "iab"], ["Ablation ladder", "ablation"]]), { value: "cross", label: t("view") })







pf_investable = pf_data ? pf_data.cross_model.models.filter((m) =&gt; m.status === "OK") : []
viewof pf_chosen = Inputs.checkbox(pf_investable.map((m) =&gt; m.id), {
  label: t("models"), value: this?.value ?? ["ipca", "qz_ipca", "naipca_iab"],
  format: (id) =&gt; pf_investable.find((m) =&gt; m.id === id).label, disabled: pf_view !== "cross"
})
viewof pf_cost = Inputs.radio([0, 10, 50], { label: t("cost"), value: this?.value ?? 10, format: (x) =&gt; `${x} bp`, disabled: pf_view === "ablation" })
viewof pf_universe = Inputs.radio(pf_data ? pf_data.iab.universes : ["CORE"], { label: t("universe"), value: this?.value ?? "CORE", disabled: pf_view !== "iab" })
viewof pf_logScale = Inputs.toggle({ label: t("log"), value: this?.value ?? true, disabled: pf_view === "ablation" })
viewof pf_sample = Inputs.radio([618, 594, 206], { label: t("sample"), value: this?.value ?? 594, disabled: pf_view !== "ablation" })












































pf_months = pf_data ? pf_data.months.map(parseMonth) : []
pf_series = {
  if (!pf_data) return []
  if (pf_view === "cross") {
    return pf_chosen.map((id) =&gt; ({ id, label: pf_investable.find((m) =&gt; m.id === id).label,
      r: netSeries(pf_data.cross_model.r[id], pf_data.cross_model.turnover[id], pf_cost) }))
  }
  if (pf_view === "iab") {
    return ["beta_only", "complete"].map((leg) =&gt; ({ id: leg, label: leg === "beta_only" ? "NA-IPCA beta-only" : "NA-IPCA complete IAB",
      r: netSeries(pf_data.iab.r[pf_universe][leg], pf_data.iab.turnover[pf_universe][leg], pf_cost) }))
  }
  return []
}
pf_rows = pf_series.flatMap((s) =&gt; wealthPath(s.r).map((w, i) =&gt; ({ date: pf_months[i], wealth: w, label: s.label, id: s.id })))























pf_ablationNames = ({ intercept_off: "Intercept off", mean_only: "Mean only", complete_iab: "Complete IAB" })
pf_ablationOrder = ["intercept_off", "mean_only", "complete_iab"]
















pf_chart = {
  if (!pf_data) return html``
  if (pf_view === "cross" && pf_chosen.length === 0) return html`&lt;p class="note"&gt;Select at least one model to draw the chart.&lt;/p&gt;`
  if (pf_view === "ablation") {
    const data = pf_data.ablation.filter((d) =&gt; d.sample_months === pf_sample)
    return Plot.plot({
      height: 260, marginLeft: 50, style: { fontFamily: "inherit", fontSize: 12 },
      ariaLabel: "Figure 1: Portfolio formation under alternative factor models, ablation ladder",
      ariaDescription: "Bar chart of gross Sharpe ratios for three input rules of one fitted model: intercept off, mean only and complete IAB.",
      x: { domain: pf_ablationOrder, tickFormat: (d) =&gt; pf_ablationNames[d], label: null },
      y: { label: "Gross Sharpe ratio", grid: true },
      marks: [
        Plot.barY(data, { x: "model", y: "gross_sharpe", fill: (d) =&gt; d.model === "complete_iab" ? palette.complete : palette.rp_pca }),
        Plot.text(data, { x: "model", y: "gross_sharpe", text: (d) =&gt; fmt2(d.gross_sharpe), dy: -8, fontFamily: "inherit" }),
        Plot.ruleY([0])
      ]
    })
  }
  const color = { domain: pf_series.map((s) =&gt; s.label), range: pf_series.map((s) =&gt; palette[s.id]) }
  return Plot.plot({
    height: 360, marginLeft: 52, style: { fontFamily: "inherit", fontSize: 12 },
    ariaLabel: "Figure 1: Portfolio formation under alternative factor models",
    ariaDescription: "Cumulative wealth from one dollar for the selected portfolio rules, June 1973 to November 2024, with NBER recessions shaded.",
    x: { label: null }, y: { type: pf_logScale ? "log" : "linear", grid: true, label: `Wealth (unit-gross, ${pf_cost} bp)` },
    color: { ...color, legend: true },
    marks: [
      nberMarks(pf_data.nber),
      Plot.lineY(pf_rows, { x: "date", y: "wealth", stroke: "label", strokeWidth: (d) =&gt; d.id === "naipca_iab" || d.id === "complete" ? 2 : 1.4 }),
      Plot.tip(pf_rows, Plot.pointerX({ x: "date", y: "wealth", stroke: "label", title: (d) =&gt; `${d.label}\n${d.date.toISOString().slice(0, 7)} · wealth ${fmt2(d.wealth)}` }))
    ]
  })
}







pf_table = {
  if (!pf_data) return html``
  if (pf_view === "cross") {
    if (pf_chosen.length === 0) return html`&lt;p class="note"&gt;Select at least one model to draw the chart.&lt;/p&gt;`
    const t = pf_data.cross_model.table.filter((d) =&gt; pf_chosen.includes(d.id))
    return html`&lt;table&gt;&lt;thead&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;Model&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Gross Sharpe&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Proxy-adjusted Sharpe (${pf_cost} bp)&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Ann. return %&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Ann. vol %&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Max drawdown %&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Turnover&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Zero-mean threshold (proxy)&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/thead&gt;
      &lt;tbody&gt;${t.map((d) =&gt; { const r = pf_data.cross_model.r[d.id], to = pf_data.cross_model.turnover[d.id]; const net = sharpe(netSeries(r, to, pf_cost));
        return html`&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;${d.label}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;${fmt2(d.gross_sharpe)}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;${fmt2(net)}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;${fmt1(d.annual_return_pct)}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;${fmt1(d.annual_vol_pct)}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;${fmt1(d.max_drawdown_pct)}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;${fmt2(d.turnover)}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;${fmtBp(d.break_even_cost_bp)}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;` })}&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
      &lt;p class="note"&gt;PCA is excluded: the release records it as degenerate (near-zero gross exposure) and not investable under the production configuration.&lt;/p&gt;`
  }
  if (pf_view === "iab") {
    const t = pf_data.iab.table.filter((d) =&gt; d.universe === pf_universe)
    const p = pf_data.iab.paired.filter((d) =&gt; d.universe === pf_universe)
    return html`&lt;table&gt;&lt;thead&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;Rule (594-month strict sample)&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Gross Sharpe&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Proxy-adjusted Sharpe (10 bp)&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Proxy-adjusted Sharpe (50 bp)&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Ann. return %&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Max drawdown %&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Turnover&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Zero-mean threshold (proxy)&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/thead&gt;
      &lt;tbody&gt;${t.map((d) =&gt; html`&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;${d.label}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;${fmt2(d.gross_sharpe)}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;${fmt2(d.net_sharpe_10bp)}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;${fmt2(d.net_sharpe_50bp)}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;${fmt1(d.annual_return_pct)}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;${fmt1(d.max_drawdown_pct)}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;${fmt2(d.turnover)}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;${fmtBp(d.break_even_cost_bp)}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;`)}&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
      &lt;table&gt;&lt;thead&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;Paired mean difference, complete − beta-only&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Months&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Monthly diff&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;95% interval&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Holm p&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/thead&gt;
      &lt;tbody&gt;${p.map((d) =&gt; html`&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;${d.sample === "STRICT24_FULL" ? "Full strict sample" : "Recent block 2007-10 onward"}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;${d.n_months}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;${(d.mean_diff_monthly * 100).toFixed(2)}%&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;[${(d.ci_low * 100).toFixed(2)}%, ${(d.ci_high * 100).toFixed(2)}%]&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;${d.p_holm &lt; 1e-4 ? "&lt; 0.0001" : d.p_holm.toFixed(4)}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;`)}&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
      &lt;p class="note"&gt;Intervals come from a 12-month block bootstrap of paired monthly returns; the Sharpe difference is descriptive.&lt;/p&gt;`
  }
  const d = pf_data.ablation.filter((x) =&gt; x.sample_months === pf_sample)
  return html`&lt;table&gt;&lt;thead&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;Input rule&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Gross Sharpe&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Ann. return %&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Ann. vol %&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Max drawdown %&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/thead&gt;
    &lt;tbody&gt;${d.map((x) =&gt; html`&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;${pf_ablationNames[x.model]}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;${fmt2(x.gross_sharpe)}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;${fmt1(x.annual_return_pct)}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;${fmt1(x.annual_vol_pct)}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;${fmt1(x.max_drawdown_pct)}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;`)}&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
    &lt;p class="note"&gt;Same fitted model throughout: the mean input, not the instability adjustment, explains most of the gross increment.&lt;/p&gt;`
}










How to read it. Cumulative wealth from one dollar on a unit-gross basis, CORE universe, June 1973 to November 2024 (618 months). Costs are applied as cost × one-way turnover per traded dollar, exactly as in the release’s tables. Hover a line for the date and value. Source: Characteristic Geometry and Portfolio Choice, research release 2026-09-09 (Characteristic_Geometry_and_Portfolio_Choice_Research_Release_2026-09-09), 03_Replication inputs core_monthly_unitgross_returns_source.csv, core_model_performance_618.csv, iab_ra_monthly.csv, beta_only_monthly.csv, Strict24_*.csv, ablation_summary.csv, nber_monthly.csv. Data · PNG · Paper page


What this shows. The ordering of the curves is the ordering of gross Sharpe ratios. Costs change levels more than ordering at 10 bp, and at 50 bp the low-turnover rules lose less. The intercept experiment is the large effect; the metric change on its own is a small one. Read the paper page for the argument.

From the release notes: cost curves are scaled-turnover sensitivity exhibits, not verified implementable net performance. Rolling geometry and input ablations are descriptive. The original stock panel is not redistributed; every number here is a portfolio-level aggregate from the public research release.
